01:09:37.000 --> 01:10:12.000
The semen staining found on Leslie's underwear could not be blood or DNA tested due to limitations with the technology. But forensic testing did conclude the staining on Leslie's underwear only contained seminal fluid, not sperm. This meant it had come from someone who was infertile. Stefan was infertile. After Stefan retracted his confession for Leslie's murder, he offered an alibi instead. On Sunday, October 5, 1975, he said he was at home between noon and 1.30pm.

